Clear the config cache with the same atomic accesses that fill it

configmap_cache holds intptr_t values but is read and filled with atomic
pointer operations, and cleared with plain integer stores. Under Fil-C an
atomic pointer store keeps its value in a side box that later atomic
loads return, so the plain stores were not observed: config changes after
the first lookup (core.abbrev, core.filemode, core.autocrlf, ...) were
ignored.
--- a/src/libgit2/config_cache.c	2026-09-26 01:20:14.075672752 +0200
+++ b/src/libgit2/config_cache.c	2026-09-26 01:20:14.076515939 +0200
@@ -136,6 +136,6 @@
 	int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < GIT_CONFIGMAP_CACHE_MAX; ++i)
-		repo->configmap_cache[i] = GIT_CONFIGMAP_NOT_CACHED;
+		(void)git_atomic_swap(repo->configmap_cache[i], (void *)GIT_CONFIGMAP_NOT_CACHED);
 }
 
